          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.091,
            0.528,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The operation done by Machine 1 is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.249,
            0.122,
            0.748,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(first number) + (second number) – (third number)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.149,
            0.846,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Written as an expression, this will be a + b – c, where a is the first number, b is the second number, and c is the third number. For example, 5 + 8 – 3 = 10, and (– 4) + (– 1) – (– 6) = 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.217,
            0.798,
            0.238
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the result of the last group will be, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( - 10) + ( - 12) - ( - 9) ="
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.251,
            0.801,
            0.316
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find the operations being done by Machine 2 and fill in the blank. Make your own machine and challenge your peers in finding its operations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.817,
            0.248,
            0.904,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.817,
                0.248,
                0.904,
                0.306
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.326,
            0.315,
            0.351
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.359,
            0.697,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the values of the following expressions: (a) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( - 5 ) \\times ( 1 8 + ( - 3 ) )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (b) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( - 7 ) \\times 4 \\times ( - 1 )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (c)\t (– 2) × (– 1) × (– 5) × (– 3)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.44,
            0.647,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Find the values of the following expressions: (a)\t (– 27) ÷ 9 "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "84 \\div ( - 4)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (c)\t (– 56) ÷ (– 2)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.52,
            0.617,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Find the integer whose product with (– 1) is: (a)\t 27 (b) – 31 (c)\t – 1 (d)\t 1 (e) 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.625,
            0.846,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "47-56+14-8+2-8+5=-4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , then find the value of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "- 4 7 + 5 6 - 1 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " + 8 – 2 + 8 – 5 without calculating the full expression."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.67,
            0.847,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Do you remember the Collatz Conjecture from last year? Try a modified version with integers. The rule is — start with any number; if the number is even, take half of it; if the number is odd, multiply it by – 3 and add 1; repeat. An example sequence is shown below."
            }
          ]
        },
